# The build context is the repo root, and the repo root contains 691 MB of live runtime
# state. Without this file every `docker build` uploads the catalogue, the 255 MB spend
# ledger and every dossier to the daemon before the first instruction runs — and worse,
# `COPY . /app` would bake a point-in-time copy of the store INTO the image, where it
# would shadow the volume mount for anything that resolved a path before the mount.
#
# The store is state. It arrives on the volume, never in the image.
store/
storage/
signals/pending/
graphify-out/

# Build outputs and dependency trees. The image installs its own.
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/bin/
**/obj/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local-only. `.env` in particular must never be baked in: secrets reach the container
# through `fly secrets` or compose's env_file, both of which keep them out of the image
# layers and out of anything that can be pulled.
.env
.env.*
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.lux/keys/
*.log

# docs/ and specs/ used to be excluded here, on the grounds that documentation is not needed
# at runtime. That stopped being true on 2026-08-19, when the console gained a Docs tab and a
# Share tab that both read the repo's own markdown. Measured on prospector-engine 2026-08-20:
# `python -m prospector.ops.console_api read docs` returned count 0 with the note "there is no
# docs/ directory in this checkout", and the tab rendered that as an empty screen. The founder
# clicked it and reported that nothing happened.
#
# The screenshots still do not travel. docs/ is 25 MB, of which docs/design/ is 22 MB of PNG
# render diffs that no console view opens; the text the console serves is 3.3 MB.
#
# tests/unit/test_the_image_ships_what_the_console_serves.py fails if a path a console read
# view resolves under is excluded again.
docs/design/
.pytest_cache/
htmlcov/
